{"id":"type-99-tank","slug":"type-99-tank","name":"Type 99","aliases":["ZTZ99","ZTZ-99","Type 99a tank","Type 99 tank"],"kind":"vehicle","category":"tanks","subcategory":"2001 Chinese main battle tank","description":"The Type 99 or ZTZ-99 is a Chinese third generation main battle tank (MBT). The vehicle was a replacement for the aging Type 88 introduced in the late 1980s. The Type 99 MBT was China's first mass-produced third-generation main battle tank. Combining modular composite armour and tandem-charge defeating ERA, 125 mm smoothbore gun with ATGM-capability, high mobility, digital systems and optics, the Type 99 represents a shift towards rapid modernization by the PLA.","history":"By 2008, 200 Type 98 and Type 99 tanks may have been deployed to the Beijing and Shenyang Military Regions. The Type 99 has seen less deployment than other tanks in PLA service due to cost factors. By 2024, more than 1,300 units of Type 99 and Type 99A have been deployed into the PLAGF service, forming the core maneuvering force of the PLA heavy combined arms brigades.","development":"The development of China's domestic third generation MBT was started in 1989, under China's eighth five-year plan. In the early 1990s China produced one of its second generation prototypes, the Type 90-II series. The Type 90-II was designed by studying the T-72 tank. The chassis was to be based on the T-72's hull but with Chinese subsystems. The Type 90-II had a 125mm smoothbore cannon with an autoloader, modular composite armor and a centered driver position. While the Type 90-II series ultimately did not enter PLA service, it saw success as an export tank and was built under license in Pakistan as the Al-Khalid.\nThe Type 98 or WZ-123 was China's domestic Type 90-II derivative. It was based on the T-72 chassis. It was first seen in rehearsals for the 1999 National Day parade and was officially revealed on 1 October 1999.\nAn improved version was shortly produced and was named the Type 98G or Type 99.\nAn updated Type 99 model was officially introduced at the 2015 Victory Day Parade as the Type 99A. This variant had previously been used by PLA troops during the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) military exercises in 2014.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Armament","items":[{"label":"Main Armament","value":"125mm ZPT-98 smoothbore gun (42 Rounds; autoloader)","numeric":125,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Secondary Armament","value":"QJC-88 heavy machine gun"},{"label":"Secondary Armament","value":"Type 86 coaxial machine gun"}]},{"group":"Protection","items":[{"label":"Armour","value":"Classified."},{"label":"Armour","value":"Anticipated to be welded turret with applique and modular composite/reactive armor"}]},{"group":"Mobility","items":[{"label":"Engine","value":"150HB liquid-cooled V12 twin-turbo diesel 33.9 litre"},{"label":"Engine Power","value":"1,500 hp (1,119 kW)","numeric":1500,"unit":"hp"},{"label":"Power/Weight","value":"27.78 hp/tonne"},{"label":"Suspension","value":"Torsion bar suspension"},{"label":"Speed (Road)","value":"76 kph"},{"label":"Speed","value":"(Type 99A)"},{"label":"Speed (Off-road)","value":"54 kph"},{"label":"Operational Range","value":"600 km–650 km","numeric":600,"unit":"km"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"51 tonnes (Type 98)","numeric":51,"unit":"tonnes"},{"label":"Weight","value":"55 tonnes (Type 99A)","numeric":55,"unit":"tonnes"},{"label":"Length (Hull)","value":"7.6 m","numeric":7.6,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Length (Gun forward)","value":"11 m","numeric":11,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Width (Hull)","value":"3.7 m","numeric":3.7,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Height (Hull)","value":"2.35 m","numeric":2.35,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Crew","value":"3 (commander, driver, gunner)"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"201st Research Institute"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Baotou Tank Plant"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1998–2001 (Type 98)"},{"label":"Produced","value":"2001–2011 (Type 99)"},{"label":"Produced","value":"2007–present (Type 99A)"},{"label":"Number Built","value":"~1,300"},{"label":"Unit Cost","value":"$2.5 million"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"China"},{"label":"In Service","value":"2001 (Type 99)"},{"label":"In Service","value":"2011–present (Type 99A)"}]}],"specIndex":{"Main Armament":"125mm ZPT-98 smoothbore gun (42 Rounds; autoloader)","Secondary Armament":"QJC-88 heavy machine gun","Armour":"Classified.","Engine":"150HB liquid-cooled V12 twin-turbo diesel 33.9 litre","Engine Power":"1,500 hp (1,119 kW)","Power/Weight":"27.78 hp/tonne","Suspension":"Torsion bar suspension","Speed":"76 kph","Operational Range":"600 km–650 km","Weight":"51 tonnes (Type 98)","Length":"7.6 m","Width":"3.7 m","Height":"2.35 m","Crew":"3 (commander, driver, gunner)","Designer":"201st Research Institute","Manufacturer":"Baotou Tank Plant","Produced":"1998–2001 (Type 98)","Number Built":"~1,300","Unit Cost":"$2.5 million","Origin":"China","In Service":"2001 (Type 99)"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/77/ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg","width":2700,"height":1800,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Tyg728"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg/330px-ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/Type_99_MBT_-_drivers_position.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Type_99_MBT_-_drivers_position.jpg","width":3572,"height":2208,"caption":"The driver position of a Type 99 tank at Shenyang training base, China.","license":"Public domain","attribution":"U.S. Air Force Staff Sgt. D. Myles Cullen"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/76/ZTZ-99A_tank_front_right_20170902.jpg","descript